Player: I found it!

What you see is an Argon Atomon.

Look carefully at its properties.

What can you observe about this element?

- It is a gas
    Correct. Argon is a gas at room temperature.

- It is a liquid
    Not quite. Argon is a gas at room temperature.

- It is a solid
    Not quite. Argon is a gas at room temperature.

Remember what you observed. Scientists use observations as evidence.